      "text": "To determine what fraction of the items on the menu you can eat, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the total number of dishes on the menu:**\n   Let \\( x \\) be the total number of dishes on the menu. According to the problem, one fifth of the menu has meatless dishes. Therefore, the number of meatless dishes is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x}{5}\n   \\]\n   We know that this number is 4 (since it is given that it is one fifth of the total number of dishes):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x}{5} = 4\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = 4 \\times 5 = 20\n   \\]\n   So, the total number of dishes on the menu is 20.\n\n2. **Determine the number of meatless dishes that are suitable for you:**\n   Out of the total number of dishes, three of the meatless dishes contain gluten. Therefore, the number of meatless dishes that are gluten-free is:\n   \\[\n   4 - 3 = 1\n   \\]\n   So, you can eat 1 meatless dish.\n\n3. **Calculate the fraction of the total menu that you can eat:**\n   The fraction of the total menu that you can eat is the number of gluten-free meatless dishes divided by the total number of dishes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{20}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{20}}\\).",
