      "text": "Let's break down the problem step-by-step to find the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat.\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dishes on the menu**:\n   We know that the dishes without meat make up one-fifth of the menu. Let the total number of dishes on the menu be \\( N \\). Then, the number of dishes without meat is \\( \\frac{1}{5}N \\).\n\n2. **Determine the number of meatless dishes**:\n   We are given that there are four dishes without meat.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{5}N = 4 \\implies N = 4 \\times 5 = 20\n   \\]\n   So, the total number of dishes on the menu is 20.\n\n3. **Identify the dishes containing gluten**:\n   We are told that three of the meatless dishes contain gluten. Since the four meatless dishes make up one-fifth of the menu, the fraction of the total menu that is meatless is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{20} = \\frac{1}{5}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, three of these four dishes contain gluten, which means that one of the meatless dishes does not contain gluten.\n\n4. **Determine the number of vegetarian options without gluten**:\n   Since three of the four meatless dishes contain gluten, there must be \\( 20 - 3 = 17 \\) vegetarian dishes in total. This includes all four meatless dishes that do not contain gluten plus any other vegetarian dishes that make up the total of 17 vegetarian options.\n\n5. **Calculate the fraction of the menu items you can eat**:\n   The number of dishes you can eat is the number of meatless dishes that do not contain gluten plus the number of vegetarian dishes. We already know there are 4 meatless dishes that do not contain gluten. Each vegetarian dish is vegetarian and may or may not be gluten-free. To find the total number of vegetarian dishes, we note that there are 17 vegetarian dishes in total and 4 of them do not contain gluten. Therefore, the number of vegetarian dishes that contain gluten is \\( 17 - 4 = 13 \\).\n\n   So, the total number of dishes you can eat is:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ (meatless dishes without gluten)} + 16 \\text{ (vegetarian dishes)} - 13 \\text{ (vegetarian dishes with gluten)} = 4 + 16 - 13 = 7\n   \\]\n\n   The fraction of the menu items that you can eat is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7}{20}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{20}}\\).",
