      "text": "My date had first stated that 4 out of the 10 total menu items are vegetarian, but didn't mention any restrictions. From the menu of 10 total items, I am able to calculate two fractions to solve the problem. First, this means that any dish that has ingredients which I am allergic to, such as pasta, is not for me. Second, I know that 3 of the vegetarian dishes contain glutens. After excluding the 4 gluten-containing dishes, I know that I have 10 - 4 = 6 options left that I can eat. To calculate the fraction of the menu I can eat, I take the number of choices left for me (vegetarian dishes without gluten) out of my original total number of options: 6/10 = 3/5. The fraction of the menu that I can eat is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}$.",
